{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/71750-a-wild-hunt","id":71750,"title":"A Wild Hunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-13T17:49:56-08:00","id":71750,"title":"A Wild Hunt","content":"So, one of my players did something very silly. For a variety of reasons, they ended up entering the Hedge in a public area with witnesses and were even caught on camera doing so. I had a character inform the group that the last time this happened, it triggered a massive Fae incursion as it drew a lot of attention to the Freehold. I fully intend to carry through with this threat, because it's quite fitting that we're on the very cusp of Summer at the moment in-game and a big battle would be a good way to kick off the season.<br /> <br /> I am a bit at a loss as to what form this Wild Hunt should take, however. A late night thunderstorm, torrential rainfall, dozens of mortals being plucked from their beds, and attacks on nearly every Changeling in the Freehold are all things that will no doubt be in the background of the event. For the players though, what do you guys think should happen? Should they just be forced to huddle in their Hollow and try to hold out until dawn? Would you draft them in to help the larger Freehold defend itself? Tell them that if they can kill the hunt's leader, the attack will end?<br /> <br /> I'm open to suggestions. Beyond kicking off the season of war, and ramming home that there are consequences for so flagrantly attracting Fae attention, I've really not got many things I feel need to happen in this attack. Your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T18:37:22-08:00","id":71772,"title":"","content":"Well, what kind of feel you want? Horror? Fantasy? Action? What is your group like? What is the general mood and themes of your game? Have they encountered fairies since their escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 02-13-2014, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T19:08:32-08:00","id":71783,"title":"","content":"Consistent mood is for, well, people that don't have to cope with a group that all want different things out of a game. Horror, fantasy, action are all things we can roll with. Members of the group range from obsessive roleplayers to a guy that built his character to be a combat-bot and likes to have something to wack each session. One player has fought his Keeper off, with the help of his Fetch, another has seen his Keeper in a dream, the group has a whole has been chased by a particularly powerful Fae in the local Hedge.<br /> <br /> When I said I was open to suggestions in the first post, I meant it. I'm open to pretty much everything. No matter what happens, someone in the group is sure to enjoy it, and the others are happy enough to put up with it long enough to get back to the things they personally enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T20:26:48-08:00","id":71801,"title":"","content":"Right now I'm feeling a chase. Each is roused from their beds by a whispering, an insistent voice drawing them together - and when they meet, a crash of lightning reveals the Horned Hunter himself, in his bloody, bare-chested, terrible glory. The Lost are given one ultimatim: Join, or be hunted. Those who join are made hounds, to be returned to Arcadia with their new master. Those who refuse are set on a terrible chase. Can they avoid, evade, or incapacitate the things which hunt them until the Hunt departs at dawn? Will the Hunter himself take them?<br /> <br /> Of course, you can always throw in a modern angle, too. Rather than a man in an antlered skull-mask riding a horse, perhaps the Huntsman is a bare-chested biker leading a fae gang of Arcadia's Angels, with antlers thrust from his biker helmet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T09:19:20-08:00","id":72023,"title":"","content":"It starts with nightmares of being chased through midnight streets by people that run like wolves. Hunched, on all fours, starved and vicious. The sound of hunting horns in the distance, growing slowly closer, is always the last image before waking up in a cold, heart pounding sweat.<br /> <br /> Changelings start avoiding sleep to keep the nightmares away. <br /> <br /> A week later, the Goblin Market vanishes like they were never there.<br /> <br /> Paranoia and fear, heightened by the shared insomnia, grips the freehold. Stories of changelings encountering groups of shambling sleepwalkers during late night walks begin to circulate. A prominent onieromancer is found one morning in a coma, the words &quot;Don't Sleep&quot; and &quot;Avoid the Thorns&quot; bloodily carved on her arms and face.<br /> <br /> It isn't long before changelings start to be attacked on the streets by the increasing amount of sleepwalkers. First by strangers, and then by friends and loved ones. Some that flee into the Hedge from these attacks are found either dead or mad and barely alive, their bodies covered with countless bite wounds. Others are not found at all.<br /> <br /> And then, in this atmosphere of exhaustion, terror and creeping insanity ... a full moon rises and the mournful blaring of distant horn echoes in the night, plunging the city into madness and darkness.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T19:49:09-08:00","id":72412,"title":"","content":"Well, that's just... beautiful. A week of fatigue penalties and siege mentality awaits.<br /> <br /> Still mulling over what exactly I want the players to do on the night of the attack itself. A chase sounds fun, particularly when coupled with the feral sleepwalkers of Firefly Night's idea. They could easily be baying hounds for a winged/mounted/motor-bike riding hunter. I can also see them taking refuge somewhere and trying to hold out until dawn. Choices, choices. I guess I should probably plan encounters for each likelihood, and roll with whatever it is the players decide to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T09:02:26-08:00","id":72653,"title":"","content":"And be ready when the players do something completely unexpected. 'Cuz they will.<br /> <br /> &quot;You... you're all joining in?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T14:24:59-08:00","id":72820,"title":"","content":"I have been running this group for a while. I know very well to expect them to do something odd, and probably suicidal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}